## Reproducibility Scope

The full production implementation of VELUM is proprietary and cannot be publicly released. It is integrated into an industrial production system and includes company-specific engineering components, internal data access layers, operational rules, and deployment infrastructure.

To support reproducibility, this repository provides:

* the anonymized Retail-IRI-1K dataset;
* the complete dataset schema;
* detailed pseudo-code for the VELUM inference procedure;
* documentation of the transition model;
* documentation of the censored-demand emission model;
* documentation of the soft stockout evidence mechanism;
* calibration details;
* the evaluation protocol used in the paper.

This release is intended to allow reviewers and researchers to inspect the dataset and independently reimplement the scientific method without exposing proprietary company code.

---

## Pseudo-Code Availability

The full production code is not released because it is company property.

Instead, the repository provides pseudo-code that describes the scientific and algorithmic structure of VELUM, including:

* prior initialization;
* transition construction;
* adaptive uncertainty calibration;
* censored sales emission;
* physical count likelihood;
* soft stockout evidence;
* Bayesian update;
* posterior normalization;
* extraction of prior and posterior medians;
* uncertainty interval computation;
* evaluation on sparse physical count dates.

The pseudo-code is intended to be sufficient for an independent academic reimplementation of the method.

---

## Usage Conditions

Retail-IRI-1K is released for academic research and reproducibility purposes.

Users of the dataset should not attempt to:

* identify the original stores;
* identify the original products;
* infer confidential commercial operations;
* reverse engineer the industrial partner's internal systems;
* use the dataset for commercial benchmarking without permission.

The dataset should be used only in ways consistent with academic research, reproducibility, and responsible data handling.

